//? Title: Image Folders: Stable Classes and Explicit Resize Geometry
//? Subtitle: Carry the training class list into every validation scan
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A folder of labelled images must become a tensor batch with stable class identities, even when a
validation folder omits a class. We generate small PNG files, scan sorted class directories and
inspect bilinear enlargement and grayscale expansion. The examples separate image geometry from
label assignment and make aspect-ratio stretching explicit.
)
\toc

> The method

scan_image_folder assigns integer labels from sorted immediate class directories, unless the
caller supplies the training class list. A validation folder containing only zebra must still label
it 1 when the training order is ant,zebra. load_image_batch gathers files and labels in requested
row order, decodes PNG/JPEG to RGB, divides by 255 and stretches to the requested height and width.
Half-pixel bilinear resizing maps output coordinate u to

$$
s(u)=\mathrm{clamp}((u+1/2)D_{\rm in}/D_{\rm out}-1/2,0,D_{\rm in}-1),\quad
v=(1-a)(1-b)v_{00}+(1-a)b v_{01}+a(1-b)v_{10}+abv_{11}.
$$
\alttext(Output pixel centres map to input centres; two fractional offsets form the four bilinear weights.)

Grayscale channels repeat into RGB; alpha is dropped. Corrupt files fail the batch rather than
silently dropping a row. Unsupported extensions are ignored by the folder scan. The scan sorts
paths; storage for a decoded batch is O(NHWC). Stretching changes aspect ratio, so use a different
crop/pad policy when that distortion would alter the task.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/image_folder_loader_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/image_folder_loader_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/image_folder_loader_concept.tikz > build/image_folder_loader_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/image_folder_loader_concept.svg build/image_folder_loader_concept.dvi > build/image_folder_loader_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/image_folder_loader_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
