> Checking the theory

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;namespace d=n::data;
 const auto folder=n::scan_image_folder("build/images");int bad=0;
 try{n::scan_image_folder("build/validation",{"ant"});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++bad;}
 d::WriteBinary("build/corrupt.png",{1,2,3});try{n::load_image_rgb("build/corrupt.png",2,2);}catch(const std::runtime_error&){++bad;}
 double channel_error=0;
 for(int width:{1,2,3,4,7}){const auto x=n::load_image_rgb(folder.images[0].path,2,width);
 for(int r=0;r<2;++r)for(int c=0;c<width;++c)for(int k=1;k<3;++k)channel_error=std::max(channel_error,std::abs(x.at({r,c,k})-x.at({r,c,0})));}
 if(bad!=2||channel_error!=0)return 1;
 std::print("Five output widths: RGB channel discrepancy {}.\n\nUnknown class and corrupt image rejected: {}.\n",channel_error,bad);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Five output widths: RGB channel discrepancy 0.

Unknown class and corrupt image rejected: 2.
// result_end


> Conclusion

Training and validation use the same class IDs despite a missing validation class. The ramp checks
the exact resize convention; grayscale expansion does not invent colour information. The fixture
covers lossless PNG loading. JPEG uses the same public batch API but has its own lossy decoding error.

> References

- [TensorFlow image resize: bilinear interpolation](https://www.tensorflow.org/api_docs/python/tf/image/resize).
- [Keras image folder loading and class names](https://keras.io/api/data_loading/image/).
